    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d755">

                <pb facs="0703" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F. 51A/4: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-25T20:00:00-04:00">April 25, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. During your forthcoming talks with the King you may state, if it appears
                    advisable to do so, as suggested in your 116, April 20, 1 p.m., that if King Ibn
                    Saud would like to have American advisers in a military, financial or other
                    capacity, sympathetic consideration will be given to his request.</p>
                <p>It appears desirable that Eddy remain in Riyadh if it is feasible to arrange for
                    him to do so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
